---
// Start: the first journey off the setup hub, and the one every other reads
// from. One screen at a time, in the setup layer: the documents the tenant
// already has, then six questions only the tenant can answer, then the answers
// read back as one sentence. Every chosen answer names the journeys it makes
// relevant, so the hub lights for the first time when this page hands off.
//
// The brief's five (docs/product-brief.md §5):
//
// 1. ONE QUESTION: "What only I can answer?" asked one screen at a time, with
//    the paperwork taken first because it answers the rest for free.
// 2. READERS: the program admin on day one. The absent reader is the staff
//    member who would otherwise type every list in by hand.
// 3. SERIES/SCALAR: a series of screens, one choice each. No scalar; the count
//    of what the documents produced belongs to the hub, not to this page.
// 4. IRREVERSIBLE: nothing. The step rail and Edit revisit any answer; the
//    bar's Finish later keeps what was answered.
// 5. CUT: a count or a percentage (the rail lists the steps by name, and the
//    hub is where progress across milestones lives), per-screen helper text,
//    and an extraction summary between the upload and the questions. The rail
//    itself came back with every milestone's (Andy, 2026-09-24).
//
// manifest:
//   layout: stack(2xl)
//   sections:
//     - milestone band -> firma2-setup-milestone-header   (rendered by SetupLayout)
//     - start steps    -> firma2-setup-start-steps   (rail of labelled steps: firma2-setup-step-rail)
import SetupLayout from '../../../layouts/SetupLayout.astro';
import Firma2SetupStartSteps from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-start-steps.astro';
---
<SetupLayout title="Start" milestone="documents">
  <div class="stack" data-gap="2xl">
    <Firma2SetupStartSteps />
  </div>
</SetupLayout>
